blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n4.4-stable\n\n### System information\n\nUbuntu 20.04\n\n### Issue description\n\nA pointer variable named new_bus_details is defined at line 1318 in the file /godot/servers/audio_server.cpp and allocated a new dynamic memory region using the new operator. At line 1325, ERR_FAIL_COND is essentially a macro definition, which causes the function to return when an if condition evaluates to true. Therefore, at this point, when the if condition evaluates to true, the function will return. At this time, the dynamic memory region pointed to by new_bus_details is neither used, as seen at line 1338, nor freed, resulting in a memory leak defect, as shown in the figure below:\nhttps://github.com/LuMingYinDetect/godot_defects/blob/main/godot_3.png\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nThe defect can be triggered by following the path provided in the figure.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nThe defect can be triggered by following the path provided in the figure.","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godot